t  like yours you see i'm a cursed  langmower long in order to violence and  death and in the case of a langmore  perhaps not soon enough there are two  lines that are omitted from this  original letter but the spirit is the  same as far as what we see in the teaser  most of the early shots are from part  one we see wyatt at the trailer and ruth  driving away after discovering the  bodies there's a new one of crime tape  on darlene's front door and a shot of  navarro in his jail cell with his door  opening nothing jumps out here he looks  like he's in the same jumpsuit that he  was wearing in the finale and you can  see that his hand still has the bandage  on it so not much time has probably  passed there's a quick shot of hobby  smiling which i think is new although  it's hard to say what's going on he  might be talking to claire shaw here  then there's one of the more interesting  shots this is the new character camila  alexandro omar navarro's sister hobby's  mother she's supposed to play a large  role in part two and in this shot we see  marty meeting with her in mexico another  interesting one has ruth turning on the  light in darlene's barn and there's a  lot of dope packaged up and ready to go  it's been a question as to what will  happen to her property and her poppy  farm and i don't know if ruth would end  up getting control of those what i  hadn't considered though was that there  may be a large amount of processed  heroin ready to go in that case what we  see here someone would have to get rid  of all of that and this would equate to  a pretty substantial windfall of cash  for ruth this makes sense because who  else would be able to make this  disappear that might give her something  to work with when she sets out to go  after hobby in the closing shot ruth is  looking at a handgun on the seat of her  truck and on the screen it says the end  arrives sooner than you think so it's an  interesting tease but it is just that a  tease it's not a lot to go off 